## 2.3 Implement arc-length-based movement

The current engine progresses along trajectories using the Bézier/ellipse parameter `u`.

Linear parameter progression does not guarantee constant screen-space velocity.

For curved Bézier trajectories, the derivative varies along the path.

Consequently, logos may move at inconsistent apparent speeds.

Implement a precomputed arc-length lookup table for each trajectory.

Suggested process:

1. Sample the trajectory at approximately 100–160 points.
2. Calculate cumulative distances.
3. Normalize the total path length.
4. Convert the time-based phase into normalized traveled distance.
5. Find the corresponding path parameter using interpolation.
6. Evaluate the actual position and tangent.

Use the same geometry evaluation for logo positioning and trajectory visualization.

This will provide more controlled, natural movement.

